  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $\u27e8x,y\u27e9={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product.",
  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016v\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8v,v\u27e9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\u2016v\u2016$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016v\u2016 & =\\sqrt{\u27e8v,v\u27e9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot 3+4\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (-2))+7\\cdot (0\\cdot 0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
